cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use this analytical code, please cite this software release."

title: "Reproducible R code for working-age mortality from ischemic heart disease in Brazil, 2015–2024"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Sardinha"
    given-names: "Daniele Melo"

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-10-21"

repository-code: "https://github.com/DanieleSardinha/ihd-brazil-working-age-2015-2024"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23547645"

license: "MIT"

abstract: >-
  Reproducible R code supporting the nationwide study of ischemic heart disease
  mortality among working-age adults in Brazil, 2015–2024. The workflow includes
  age-standardized mortality rates with corrected variance estimation, temporal
  trend analyses, sex- and region-specific estimates, sociodemographic
  distributions, years of potential life lost, assessment of ill-defined causes
  of death, hospital utilization and SUS reimbursement analyses, and
  mortality-related productivity losses. Individual-level source and derived
  datasets are not redistributed; the repository provides analytical scripts,
  documentation, and aggregated reproducibility outputs.
